From 67566b07cb21821799d99d4e3c2774e4e3a43c2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Orlitzky <michael@orlitzky.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Jul 2021 08:01:46 -0400
Subject: Trac #32037: update the doctest for the DirichletGroup(5)[1]
 L-function.

Due to a change in libLfunction's API, this L-function is now
automatically determined to be complex, which means that we search for
zeros below the real axis as well. As a result, the first zero (in
magnitude) is now negative. (In the past, it was ignored without
do_negative=True). We update the doctest to include it.
