From 22efbb4807a20aa4ff10a8b6b2d17d9157778e86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Orlitzky <michael@orlitzky.com>
Date: Thu, 25 Nov 2021 11:07:46 -0500
Subject: Trac #32037: don't use "abs tol" for complex numbers.

Our "abs tol" doctest test modifier doesn't really handle complex
numbers, and only works incidentally when both components are parsed
into equal-length lists of floats. And moreover, doctest decorators
aren't fully appropriate in EXAMPLES, because the user can't reproduce
them. In this commit we replace a bunch of "abs tol" examples in
the sage.lcalc.lcalc_Lfunction module with explicit ones.
---
